// PumpOutputImpedance: the impedance the HC electrode sees looking back into the pump,
// with the HC guard connected (SPEC.md, "Guard loop stability"). The drive input is
// held at 0 V and a 1 uA test current is pushed into E_HC, so V(E_HC) / 1 uA is the
// pump's output impedance in parallel with the HC node's strays. The HC strays are
// those of SoilSweep: 20 pF from the node to its guard, 0.3 pF to ground, 100 pF from
// the guard to the ground layer. The electrodes are in air: nothing else loads E_HC.
//
// The sweep runs to 1 GHz, past the loop crossovers, because peaking shows there.
// SPEC.md sets no requirement on the output impedance itself (the current is
// measured, so it only sets how much of the current reaches the soil); the limits
// are derived in README.md ("PumpOutputImpedance"):
//  - guard loop: the guard driver feeds the node back through CG_HC, a positive
//    feedback loop with gain |V(GUARD_HC) / V(E_HC)| * CG / C_total, C_total = 21.3 pF
//    (20 pF to the guard, 0.3 pF residual, 1 pF of U_FBB's input). It is stable
//    with the electrodes in air while the tracking stays below 21.3 / 20 = 1.065;
//  - at least 1.5 Mohm at 1 kHz, ten times the largest drive impedance, so that at
//    least 90 % of the set current reaches the soil at the bottom of the band.
// Reported without a limit: a guard that lags its node gives the node a negative real
// part (negative_conductance_vs_load compares it with the conductance of the largest
// drive impedance, 160 kohm). It was first written with a limit of -50 %, failed by
// three orders of magnitude above the band, and turned out to be the wrong test:
// README.md, "PumpOutputImpedance", explains why and what would settle stability.
// The 1 MHz value is reported: there the pump feeds its own strays and the soil
// current falls (SoilSweep, soil_current_1mhz), which costs signal, not accuracy.
bench PumpOutputImpedance for AnalogFrontEnd using FrontEndPorts {
    model DDS: source { out = DDS_OUT; ref = GND; ac = 0V; output_resistance = 200ohm; }   // drive held at 0 V
    replace J_PROBE with source { out = E_HC; ref = GND; output = current; ac = 1uA; }

    component CG_HC: CAPACITOR { value = 20pF; }
    component C0_HC: CAPACITOR { value = 0.3pF; }
    component GG_HC: CAPACITOR { value = 100pF; }
    net E_HC { CG_HC.1; C0_HC.1; }
    net GUARD_HC { CG_HC.2; GG_HC.1; }
    net GND { C0_HC.2; GG_HC.2; }

    analysis ac { from = 1kHz; to = 1GHz; points_per_decade = 20; }

    let z_out = V(E_HC) / 1uA;
    measure guard_loop_tracking = max(mag(V(GUARD_HC) / V(E_HC))) { max = 106%; }
    measure negative_conductance_vs_load = min(re(1 / z_out)) * 160kohm;
    measure min_real_part = min(re(z_out));
    measure z_out_1khz = mag(at(z_out, 1kHz)) { min = 1.5Mohm; }
    measure z_out_100khz = mag(at(z_out, 100kHz));
    measure z_out_1mhz = mag(at(z_out, 1MHz));
    measure peak_z_out = max(mag(z_out));
    // The guard follows the node: their ratio shows how well the HC guard is driven.
    measure guard_tracking_1mhz = mag(at(V(GUARD_HC) / V(E_HC), 1MHz));
    plot mag(z_out), re(z_out), phase(z_out), mag(V(GUARD_HC) / V(E_HC));
}
